Reconstruct a numerical geological history with analytical and model uncertainty (@geo-time-project: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @geology, #source "../sources/Introduction-to-Geochronology-Vermeesch.lingua#r_30AEAXYK3VV89FDX1TF9ZKJ84J", #source "../sources/IsoplotR-Vermeesch.lingua#r_6H156FG6EJ2M5AJ1A9GV0NV3S4", #source "../sources/International-Stratigraphic-Guide.lingua#r_6NAYJE2KFXGRNCWP6TEY7AZE7J", #source "../../../../hephaestus/inquiry/reproducible-computation/Reproducible-computation.lingua#r_78FWWJDCV0ZGG7VYSPRCWN56DQ", #geology "Advanced-structural-and-plate-reconstruction.lingua#r_0TZDDE53WP7NTCMNE0D5VB4EMC") { r_4WC3HDHSNQKQ941M1S0VY8HJR3
**Read:** [Introduction to Geochronology — Pieter Vermeesch](../sources/Introduction-to-Geochronology-Vermeesch.lingua#r_30AEAXYK3VV89FDX1TF9ZKJ84J), the complete notes, exercises, and practicals; [IsoplotR: A free and open toolbox for geochronology — Vermeesch](../sources/IsoplotR-Vermeesch.lingua#r_6H156FG6EJ2M5AJ1A9GV0NV3S4), the complete article and the relevant supplement; [International Stratigraphic Guide, abridged version — ICS](../sources/International-Stratigraphic-Guide.lingua#r_6NAYJE2KFXGRNCWP6TEY7AZE7J), all unit/correlation principles used; [Reproducible computational work](../../../../hephaestus/inquiry/reproducible-computation/Reproducible-computation.lingua#r_78FWWJDCV0ZGG7VYSPRCWN56DQ), the full relevant reproducibility and independent-check studies.

Read all of Vermeesch's geochronology notes, exercises, and programming practicals, following mathematical/analytical preparation where required. Read the complete IsoplotR paper and relevant supplement. The aim is to explain how observations become ages and histories, not simply run a package on a column of values.

Choose an authorized published study with accessible methods/data and a question involving growth, eruption, deposition, metamorphism, cooling, or exposure. Trace sample context, separation/preparation, analytical calibration, isotopic observations, correction, constants, covariance, regression, and geological interpretation. Identify what event each age can constrain.

Independently reproduce one age/isochron or other selected reduction with explicit uncertainty and numerical checks. Compare with the published result and an appropriate independently implemented method. Preserve software/data versions and identify correlated systematic components instead of treating all observations as independent.

**Work:** test an alternative involving inheritance, open-system behavior, mixing, reworking, excess scatter, or a changed thermal/history model, as applicable. Determine which observations distinguish it. Explain whether an age difference is resolved after shared uncertainty and whether the available evidence supports an event duration or only ordering/bounds.

Produce a substantive methods/results/discussion account and defend it against an independent critique. Propose a feasible new measurement or sampling design that would resolve the principal ambiguity. No future laboratory result is claimed here: actual analytical competence requires suitable supervised instrument and sample work beyond interpreting supplied data.

**Continue:** [Test a regional reconstruction against geometry, ages, and competing models](Advanced-structural-and-plate-reconstruction.lingua#r_0TZDDE53WP7NTCMNE0D5VB4EMC).

**Return:** [Geology — Earth materials, processes, history, and investigation](../Geology.lingua#r_3CK43VQS79NK0STWNPSCS8YM06).
